{"kind":"human_teaching","topic":"cash-spawn-and-generator-fragment-failure","fact":"In a recent merge anomaly, a green cash item was visibly generated while the system also attempted to merge General Generator Card Lvl.1 with Lvl.2 and failed. When the cause of missing free-cell gain is unclear and green candidates are present, select the green item and read its top hint to identify whether it is the cash-stack item instead of inferring from color alone.","source":"operator_question_answer","status":"promoted"}
{"kind":"implementation_learning","topic":"energy-spend-without-orders","fact":"If the customer strip is temporarily unreadable/empty but a visible producer is already known and board capacity is available, bounded producer output is preferable to idling when the active objective is to spend safe game energy. Unknown producers remain excluded from blind production.","source":"live-play-bottleneck","status":"promoted"}
{"kind":"human_teaching","topic":"general-generator-card-priority","fact":"For the current play objective, General Generator Card fragments are low priority and should be ignored rather than actively pursued. Do not spend merge/analysis effort on them unless needed for board safety or a later explicit objective.","source":"operator","status":"promoted"}
{"kind":"human_teaching","topic":"merge-anomaly-level-verification","fact":"When a merge anomaly cannot be explained by an observed bubble, green cash-stack spawn, or other added object, verify the attempted items' semantic identity/level before retrying. If the levels/identities differ, treat the visual pair as a recognition mistake and tighten discrimination for that confusing appearance instead of repeatedly dragging it.","source":"operator","status":"promoted"}
{"kind":"observation","topic":"merge-lookalike-confirmed-level-mismatch","fact":"Live verification of the repeatedly anomalous pair r1c1/r3c6 showed r1c1 = ゼネラルジェネレータカードのいくつかの断片 Lvl.1, while r3c6 = ゼネラルジェネレータカードの断片 Lvl.2. They are visually similar but not mergeable. Repeated non-progressing visual pairs should be temporarily suppressed and escalated to semantic/level confirmation rather than repeatedly dragged.","source":"live-device-panel-ocr","status":"promoted"}
{"e":"U","k":"merge.outcome-image-diff-candidate","v":{"status":"candidate","principle":"when free-cell count after a merge differs from the expected gain, compare the pre/post board images at cell/ROI level to identify which cells actually changed instead of inferring only from counts","use_for":["bubble spawn","green cash spawn","merge no-op","other random spawn","animation contamination"],"implementation_direction":"prefer per-cell/ROI visual deltas from the already captured pre/post frames before escalating to OCR or a human question; preserve the changed-cell evidence with the question if ambiguity remains","source":"human_teaching","date":"2026-08-22"}}
{"e":"D","k":"perception.empty-cell-background-reference.20260822","v":{"status":"candidate-validated","observation":"producer glow can leak into neighboring empty cells and make their outer crop look occupied/mergeable","live_evidence":{"false_pair":["r6c3","r6c6"],"deep_center_content_scores":[1.031,1.116],"empty_background_rgb":[223,220,197]},"method":"classify occupancy from a deep center crop plus calibrated board-background color distance; keep sprite similarity on a wider crop","reason":"variance alone can misclassify flat-color real items as empty, while color distance separates those from the pale board tile","source":"live_play+tests","date":"2026-08-22"}}
